{
  "category": "Grass Quill Pokémon",
  "entries": [
    {
      "text": "This wary Pokémon uses photosynthesis to store up energy during the day, while becoming active at night.",
      "version": "sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "Silently it glides, drawing near its targets. Before they even notice it, it begins to pelt them with vicious kicks.",
      "version": "moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "It sends its feathers, which are as sharp as blades, flying in attack. Its legs are strong, so its kicks are also formidable.",
      "version": "ultra-sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "It feels relaxed in tight, dark places and has been known to use its Trainer’s pocket or bag as a nest.",
      "version": "ultra-moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "At a distance, it launches its sharp feathers while flying about. If the enemy gets too close, Rowlet switches tactics and delivers vicious kicks.",
      "version": "sword"
    },
    {
      "text": "During the day, it builds up energy via photosynthesis. At night, it flies silently through the sky, on the prowl for prey.",
      "version": "shield"
    },
    {
      "text": "Flies noiselessly on delicate wings. It has mastered the art of deftly launching dagger-sharp feathers from those same wings.",
      "version": "legends-arceus"
    }
  ],
